# Curious Obsession on an opponent's creature: the granted "Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, you may
# draw a card" is the creature's ability, so "you" is its controller (CR 113.8, 603.3a): Bot2's enchanted Savannah Lions (3/2)
# hits Bot1 on turn 4 and Bot2 draws (library 11 -> 10), Bot1 draws nothing. The end-step sacrifice is the Aura's
# controller's: Bot1 attacked on turn 3 (Bot2 had no creature then), Bot2's turn 4 end step is not Bot1's, so the Aura is
# still on the Lions on turn 5; on turn 5 Bot1 attacks with nothing and sacrifices it into its own graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Savannah Lions
Curious Obsession
Plains x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Savannah Lions
Plains x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Savannah Lions.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Savannah Lions.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Savannah Lions > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Curious Obsession.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Savannah Lions)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Savannah Lions.Power = 3
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Savannah Lions > Bot1)
[T4 Bot2.CombatDamage]
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Accept
[T4 Bot2.End]
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Curious Obsession.AttachedTo = Savannah Lions
? Bot2.Library.Count = 10
? Bot1.Library.Count = 11
[T5 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 17
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot2.Library.Count = 10
Bot1.Library.Count = 11
Bot1.Battlefield.Curious Obsession = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard = Curious Obsession
